+    {
+      "topic": "job_protocol",
+      "detail": "repository.py declares keyword-only acquire/heartbeat/CAS inputs; retry_job is concrete SQLite API, absent from SimulationJobRepository Protocol. Exact signatures in files."
+    },
+    {
+      "topic": "job_guard",
+      "detail": "publication_guard is per resolved DB/PID RLock + flock with same-thread reentry, yields None; it is not a transaction receipt. acquire is wrapped, heartbeat/release are not. acquire calculates now/deadline before BEGIN IMMEDIATE; heartbeat samples now after BEGIN IMMEDIATE and rowcount1 rejects dead/cancelled/mismatched lease."
+    },
+    {
+      "topic": "memory_jobs",
+      "detail": "InMemorySimulationJobRepository subclasses SQLiteSimulationJobRepository and owns TemporaryDirectory/runtime.db; close cleans its temporary directory. SQLite _connect is isolation_level=None and finally explicitly closes per-call connection."
+    },
+    {
+      "topic": "event_transactions",
+      "detail": "Memory uses nonreentrant threading.Lock; SQLite uses nonreentrant _write_lock and persistent _conn. Bootstrap/supervision/publication/routing writes derive/check under event repository lock; SQLite writes BEGIN IMMEDIATE. Typed transition request normalization precedes lock. There is currently no shared job/event transaction authority parameter."
+    },
+    {
+      "topic": "worker_private_origin",
+      "detail": "poll_once acquire -> heartbeat thread -> _execute -> finally heartbeat.join(timeout=1), release and revoke. _execute takes publication_guard and real start_attempt; after RUNNING it calls _prepare_startup/from_worker/_begin_origin then records original monotonic/UTC tuple and seals it before _run/RESET/settle. Late _new_handoff binds source+limits; runtime consumes via exact binding and actual backend episode _consume_handoff, token popped once. Public WorkerRuntimeSource alone does not authorize new owner."
+    },
+    {
+      "topic": "recovery",
+      "detail": "ArtifactRecoveryService.recover_interrupted_jobs expires leases first, under publication_guard verifies current snapshot identity, finishes open attempts and CASes INTERRUPTED to RECOVERY_PENDING; requeue only explicit flag. service.start recovers before dispatcher.start. SQLite retry retains job identity/manifest/repro hash but clears lease/worker/cancel; new attempt authority cannot reuse ended owner."
+    },
+    {
+      "topic": "skill_entry",
+      "detail": "vision/execution.py dispatches to raw_recorder.execute_attempt or edge.runtime.skill_executor.SkillExecutor.execute_attempt. Runtime definition.handler(robot, validated_parameters, step.timeout_ms) is the actual submission boundary after preconditions. edge/skill_executor.py is legacy execute_step; covering only it misses normal runtime."
+    },
+    {
+      "topic": "backend_three_branches",
+      "detail": "MuJoCoPhysicsBackend.step: operation observer branch -> control/actuator/_advance_observed_physics_step; no physics observer branch -> control/actuator/mj_step; physics observer branch -> control/actuator/mj_step/callback. _apply_control dequeues due pending targets and writes arm ctrl; apply_joint_targets mutates queue or targets; apply_gripper_command writes gripper ctrl. Guards needed at actual consumption must cover all branches, queue consumption and gripper."
+    },
+    {
+      "topic": "observer_lifetime",
+      "detail": "All observer contexts unregister in finally; physics/actuator allow one current observer and prohibit backend mutation/reentrant stepping in callbacks. Operation hook is independent read-only recording with retained failure/allocation ledger, not dispatch permission. Recorder enters operation context and flushes/finally exits; purpose and execute_attempt retain interval/error disposition."
+    },
+    {
+      "topic": "clock_source",
+      "detail": "ExperimentClock measures monotonic elapsed and maps request waits to physics advance. RawRecorderV3 _clock_pair samples monotonic_ns before/after independent UTC reading; purpose interval allocates before side-effect work and closes in finally. Existing interval evidence does not itself confer mutation authority."
+    },
